(ned TCP CAL -- ONE STEP of the automated convergence, operator 2026-08-05)
(Sequence the operator specified: park ~10 mm over the puck, press START,)
(and the machine walks A up in small steps, improving L at each one.)
(Each step: rotate A, RETURN TO THE ORIGINAL START POSE, probe down.)
(The return is not cosmetic -- with tool-tip kins live, commanding the)
(same tool-tip XYZ puts the TIP back where it started whatever A is, so)
(any drift in Y from a wrong pivot is corrected before every probe.)
(The A=0 reference Z is taken ONCE and never re-measured: that number)
(does not change, so re-touching it only adds noise.)
(35 deg is the ceiling -- past that the rod RADIUS contacts before the)
(needle tip and the measurement stops being about the tip.)
(EVERY position here is the interpreter own reading from a previous)
(probe -- #5061/#5062/#5063. Nothing is reconstructed from stat: that)
(is what sent a probe to machine -959 and refused to move.)
(Args: #1 = target A in degrees)
(      #2 = 1 to reposition to the start pose first, 0 for the first probe)
(      #3 = start X   #4 = start Y   #5 = start Z, all tool-tip work frame)
(      #6 = plunge depth in mm; 0 or less = MOVE ONLY, do not probe)
(      #7 = puck: 1 raise and dwell before probing, -1 retract at the end,)
(           0 leave it as it is. THE PUCK MUST BE UP BEFORE ANY PLUNGE --)
(           it was missing entirely and the first sweep plunged onto a)
(           retracted puck, 2026-08-05.)
o<tcp_auto_step> sub
  #<targa>  = #1
  #<repos>  = #2
  #<sx>     = #3
  #<sy>     = #4
  #<sz>     = #5
  #<plunge> = #6
  #<puck>   = #7
  #<fast>   = 200.0
  #<latch>  = 10.0
  #<back>   = 1.0
  #<trav>   = 1500.0

  o10 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, TCP AUTO: switch to MM first - this routine is metric)
  o10 endif
  o16 if [ABS[#<targa>] GT 35]
    (abort, TCP AUTO: A beyond 35 deg - the rod radius would touch first)
  o16 endif

  M50 P0

  ; PUCK UP FIRST, and give the pneumatics their settle time. There is no
  ; deployed sensor, so the dwell IS the proof -- same 1.5 s the puck
  ; centre cycle uses. Nothing below may plunge before this has run.
  o18 if [#<puck> GT 0]
    M64 P3
    G4 P1.5
  o18 endif

  o20 if [#<repos> GT 0]
    G90
    ; rotate FIRST, at the safe start height, then put the TIP back on the
    ; start pose. With a wrong pivot the tilt moves the tip; this move is
    ; what pulls it back over the puck.
    G1 A#<targa> F1000
    G1 X#<sx> Y#<sy> Z#<sz> F[#<trav>]
  o20 endif

  o30 if [#<plunge> GT 0]
    G91
    G38.2 Z-#<plunge> F[#<fast>]
    G1 Z[#<back>] F[#<trav>]
    G38.2 Z-[#<back> + 1.0] F[#<latch>]
    #<xt> = #5061
    #<yt> = #5062
    #<zt> = #5063
    #<at> = #5064
    G38.5 Z[#<back> + 1.0] F[#<latch>]
    G90
    G1 Z#<sz> F[#<trav>]
  o30 endif
  ; A BACK TO ZERO BEFORE THE GUI APPLIES THE NEW PIVOT. Changing
  ; pivot-length steps the inverse solution by dL*sin[A] in Y and
  ; dL*[1-cos A] in Z -- at A=-24 deg a 160 mm correction commanded a 66 mm
  ; joint jump in one servo cycle and threw following errors on four joints
  ; (2026-08-05, by hand, guard bypassed). At A=0 the pivot cancels out of
  ; the solution entirely, so the write costs nothing.
  G1 A0 F1000
  ; puck DOWN at the end of the sequence -- an energised solenoid bleeds
  ; the air supply down, learned 2026-08-02 the hard way
  o40 if [#<puck> LT 0]
    M65 P3
    G4 P1.5
  o40 endif
  M50 P1
  o50 if [#<plunge> GT 0]
    (DEBUG, EVAL[vcp.getWidget{"ned_controls"}.tcp_auto_point{#<xt>, #<yt>, #<zt>, #<at>}])
  o50 endif
o<tcp_auto_step> endsub
M2
